# Fixed IPP Identify-Printer request used by the catalog action printer.identify (docs/printer.md).
# Managed by ahlikoding.com and satpamsiber.com under ahliweb.com.
#
# Asks the printer to flash its display and sound a beep so the operator can tell which one it is. It sends no name,
# address, serial or job data; the printer URI is the only variable and the repair engine builds it from the CUPS
# queue of the printer it resolved (ipp://localhost/printers/QUEUE). A printer or driver that does not implement
# Identify-Printer answers operation-not-supported and the action reports a failed step; nothing else happens.
{
	NAME "rescue identify printer"
	OPERATION Identify-Printer
	GROUP operation-attributes-tag
	ATTR charset attributes-charset utf-8
	ATTR language attributes-natural-language en
	ATTR uri printer-uri $uri
	ATTR keyword identify-actions display,sound
	STATUS successful-ok
	STATUS successful-ok-ignored-or-substituted-attributes
}
